{% extends "_base.j2" %}
{% block main %}
<span class="eyebrow">Learn · generation assets</span><h1>Fuzz corpora</h1><p class="lede">DWARF currently inventories {{ corpus_count }} explicit corpus units containing {{ input_count }} inputs. Corpora are retained bytes fed to real target implementations; they are not simulated node behavior.</p>
<div class="definition-actions"><a class="cta" href="/operate/corpora">Browse corpora</a><a class="cta cta--ghost" href="/api/corpora/export" download>Download all</a></div><hr class="hairline">
<section><span class="eyebrow">Roles</span><h2>One byte string can have different lifecycle roles</h2><div class="testcase-term-grid"><article class="learn-tile"><span class="learn-tile__eyebrow">Seed</span><p>An initial, intentionally small input used to start mutation.</p></article><article class="learn-tile"><span class="learn-tile__eyebrow">Generated</span><p>An input produced from a structure-aware generator such as Cuddle/CDDL.</p></article><article class="learn-tile"><span class="learn-tile__eyebrow">Queue</span><p>A fuzzer-retained input that expanded coverage or behavior.</p></article><article class="learn-tile"><span class="learn-tile__eyebrow">Crash</span><p>Bytes associated with abnormal target termination; evidence to triage, not automatically a vulnerability.</p></article><article class="learn-tile"><span class="learn-tile__eyebrow">Minimized</span><p>A smaller input proven to preserve a selected behavior.</p></article><article class="learn-tile"><span class="learn-tile__eyebrow">Regression</span><p>A reviewed input retained so a known behavior remains continuously testable.</p></article><article class="learn-tile"><span class="learn-tile__eyebrow">Promoted</span><p>A testcase artifact deliberately copied into the writable runtime overlay.</p></article></div></section>
<section><span class="eyebrow">Lifecycle</span><h2>Discover → inspect → exercise → retain → promote</h2><ol><li>DWARF inventories only the shipped <code>dwarf/corpora/</code> tree and the configured runtime overlay.</li><li>Each exact input gets a size, SHA-256, duplicate group, safe bounded preview, and download.</li><li>Scenarios and target manifests establish relationships only when their source explicitly references the corpus.</li><li>Interesting queue/crash inputs enter the testcase lifecycle; review and minimization happen before promotion.</li><li>A promoted regression seed is copied atomically into the writable overlay. Shipped repository corpora stay immutable.</li></ol></section>
<section><span class="eyebrow">Schema and safety</span><h2>Supported records and writes</h2><p>The generated catalog record validates against <code>dwarf/spec/v1/corpus-record.schema.json</code>. Optional <code>corpus.json</code> metadata can declare role, provenance, source campaign, target IDs, grammar IDs, and status; malformed metadata remains visible as a diagnostic.</p><p>The browser is a corpus-management surface, <strong>not an arbitrary binary editor</strong>. Binary content is uploaded/downloaded as exact bytes. Text previews are escaped. CBOR previews are bounded hexadecimal bytes, not a claim that the target accepted or semantically decoded the value; the real target decoder remains authoritative. Imports are limited to 1 MiB; all mutations are POST-only and token-gated; bad requests write nothing; duplicate detection is SHA-256 based; removal is recoverable under <code>.trash/</code>.</p><p>Noise such as <code>._*</code>, <code>.DS_Store</code>, cache directories, and bytecode is excluded from inventory and export.</p></section>
<section><span class="eyebrow">Examples</span><h2>Supported operator actions</h2>{% for example in examples %}<article class="concept-entry"><h3>{{ example.title }}</h3><p>{{ example.description }}</p><pre><code>{{ example.example }}</code></pre></article>{% endfor %}</section>
{% endblock %}
